   "en": "§ The mishna teaches: If «both of» the witnesses «denied» knowledge of the incident «together,» both of them «are liable.» The Gemara asks: «But» isn’t it «impossible» for two events «to coincide precisely?» By necessity, one denial must have preceded the other."
